From 3bf0715da40cc83054a6fcb78e8645466d9c3916 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 675/676] perf(dsv41): exchange directly at four ranks on a
 switched fabric

At four ranks the rank-order reduce-scatter's chunk exchange
(tilelang/collectives.py exchange_into, which sequence-parallel prefill's
row exchange also uses) and PyNCCL's all_to_all_rows relay half of the
opposite rank's block through each neighbour: on sparknet's switchless
four-node ring, ranks two apart share no cable. Behind a switch every pair
is one hop, and the relay costs a second serialized group and 4 instead of
3 chunk-units sent per rank.

ring4_relay() now drops the relay only when sparknet renders the direct
topology (SPARKNET_ROCE_TOPOLOGY=direct, as tp4-switched does); every rank
then sends to and receives from every other in one group, the path other
world sizes already take. Any other value, or none, keeps the relay, which
works on every fabric. Since candidate-35's 0669, exchanges sparknet's
one-shot accepts (since candidate-36, single-slot messages) go there first;
this changes the PyNCCL path the larger prefill exchanges still take.

Base: candidate-36's vLLM series (vllm 19f2c20e + 0001..0673, expected
tree cc0fdf58); with this patch, tree bc7c9cd5.

Quality: only bytes move. The rank-order sum and every part are the same
bits, so outputs are unchanged. Measured on four GB10 behind one switch
(MikroTik CRS804-4DDQ) on candidate-36 against candidate-36's own two
files, two boots each at the recipe's 16,384-token budget: prefill +3.2%
to +3.4% at 32K-256K, closed-loop decode unchanged, engine grid -0.16%
+-1.05% over boots; greedy token ids and every teacher-forced top-20
distribution identical (KL 0); no RDMA error counter grew on any HCA.
On spark-ds41f-1030 the same change read prefill +2.7%.

Tests: tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_collectives.py gains a
switched fabric (every pair linked) and checks that four ranks exchange
with every peer in one group per exchange with the relay's bits, and that
every other SPARKNET_ROCE_TOPOLOGY value keeps the ring relay;
tests/models/test_deepseek_v41_sp_project_reduce_scatter.py runs
all_to_all_rows on both topologies. On GB10 (release-test runner, the 10
gate files that exercise the exchange): 822 passed, 1 failed, 1 skipped,
every new or changed case passed; the one failure (a disk-Engram
preparation test) fails identically without this patch.

Upstream status: local to spark-ds41f; not proposed to vLLM (the relay
and sparknet's topology are this deployment's).
